  "Name": "NBA Live 13",
  "Overview": "NBA Live 13 was the cancelled basketball installment in the NBA Live series, developed and published by Electronic Arts (EA).[1] The game was to be a reboot of the series and would be departing from previous entries, with the focus on an \"all-new experience that captures on the future of basketball\". NBA Live 13 was to be released for Xbox 360 and PlayStation 3.[2][3] There were reports that the game could have been released digitally.[4] However, on September 27, 2012, EA confirmed on their website that the game's launch has been cancelled due to the game's \"disappointing\" development.[5] EA Vice President Andrew Wilson said the company would focus on the quality of the next year's title.[5]",
